# Malrynth code ownership.
#
# ADVISORY ONLY at present. Enforcement requires branch protection with required review,
# which is unavailable for private repositories on GitHub Free (see
# docs/operations/github-ownership.md). This file is written with a future-compatible layout
# so that enabling enforcement is a settings change, not a rewrite.
#
# When an organisation exists, replace @macmma322 with team handles
# (e.g. @malrynth/kernel) -- the paths below are already grouped for that.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                                   @macmma322

# --- Privileged code: highest review bar -------------------------------------
# Everything under core/ runs with full authority or decides what does.
/core/                              @macmma322
/core/kernel/                       @macmma322
/core/kernel/src/arch/              @macmma322
/core/boot/                         @macmma322
# The handoff ABI is a contract between two privileged components; changes here
# can silently corrupt a kernel, so it is called out separately from core/.
/core/abi/                          @macmma322

# --- Governance: changes here change the rules themselves --------------------
/docs/constitution/                 @macmma322
/docs/adr/                          @macmma322
/docs/security/                     @macmma322
/docs/legal/                        @macmma322
/GOVERNANCE.md                      @macmma322
/SECURITY.md                        @macmma322
/THIRD_PARTY.md                     @macmma322
/THIRD_PARTY_POLICY.md              @macmma322

# --- Supply chain and build integrity ----------------------------------------
/.github/                           @macmma322
/.github/workflows/                 @macmma322
/tools/                             @macmma322
/Cargo.lock                         @macmma322
/rust-toolchain.toml                @macmma322
/.cargo/                            @macmma322

# --- CODEOWNERS protects itself ----------------------------------------------
# Without this, anyone able to edit CODEOWNERS can remove every rule above.
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @macmma322
